From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicola Ferralis <ferralis@generalflash.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 00:02:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ext: sketches on planes at any angle (bores, pins, windows;
 family and suite "angled")

An intent may lie on a plane at any orientation: its in-plane x direction (ux, uy, uz) marks it,
with the plane's unit normal (nx, ny, nz) and origin (x, y, z). The profile is drawn in the
plane's own frame (circles and rectangles centred on the origin, outlines in (u, v) about it) and
extruded both ways, as on an origin plane with an offset. The model issues the same commands as
for an origin plane: the runtime attaches the sketch to the XY plane with an AttachmentOffset that
carries the frame, and the sketch's normal is in the state the model sees. New family and suite
"angled" (box or cylinder with bores, pins and windows tilted 15-60 degrees). The goal encoding
gains u and a flag (EXT_NUM_DIM 31; rows stay 64 wide). Earlier suites keep their goals.
